{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ominous-indecisive-cornsnake","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nAfter landing code-review-only criterion `project.review-phase-boundaries`, fresh plan review for story 9447-b31c-e0b7-446d fails before LLM execution. `plan_review.registry.effective_criteria(repo_root)` calls the shared overlay with `gate_key=\"plan_review\"`; the global `activate` list contains the code-review-only criterion, and overlay validation raises `CriteriaError: activated criterion ... has no plan_review routing entry`. The deterministic layer catches and skips project criteria, leaving `review-plan` unsigned INDETERMINATE.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Define cross-gate activation semantics in the shared project-criteria overlay: an activated criterion routed exclusively to another known gate is ignored by the current gate, not treated as malformed.\n- Preserve strict failure for an activated id absent from every supported gate and for malformed routing in the selected gate.\n- Add regression coverage using a repository overlay with one plan-review criterion and one code-review-only criterion, exercising both registries and the real plan-review precheck path.\n- Document the gate-scoped activation behavior in the project-criteria architecture documentation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] With `activate` containing a valid code-review-only project criterion, `effective_criteria(repo_root, gate_key=\"plan_review\")` returns plan-review criteria without raising and does not include the code-review-only id.\n- [ ] With `activate` containing a valid plan-review-only project criterion, `effective_criteria(repo_root, gate_key=\"code_review\")` returns code-review criteria without raising and does not include the plan-review-only id.\n- [ ] An activated criterion absent from every supported gate still raises `CriteriaError`; malformed routing for the selected gate still raises.\n- [ ] A regression test proves `review-plan` can execute its deterministic project-criteria resolution on the landed mixed-gate overlay instead of becoming unsigned INDETERMINATE.\n- [ ] The gate-scoped activation rule is documented and canonical lint, typecheck, and test gates pass.\n- [ ] The change lands on `main` through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments.","id":"3ba4-c0d1-1813-44a5","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["project-criteria","plan-review","code-review","regression"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Scope project-criterion activation to its review gate"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785030858658950001,"uuid":"b7a45c39-5411-445f-ab01-10d2b9674e2f"}